    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Review correction: Cubic 4166190212 reproduces a second-stage settings open race after real entry validation. New tests preserve native filesystem results and perform real unlink/ancestor replacement; baseline fails ENOENT and ENOTDIR, fixed canonical settings owner passes 49/49, while native EACCES/ELOOP still reject. The existing preview bootstrap matrix now uses a genuine spawned dist/cli.js completion path for no-extensions cases; a launcher-only exit-17 control fails the revised existing tests and passed the original. SDK wording now identifies the plan-requested ID and limits decoration to PmCliError inspect/prepare/apply failures, preserving native and compensation/recovery semantics. Fresh shared-source linked tests, exact coverage, documentation and strict gates will be produced before publication. All prior failed receipts remain failed; old fb7 coverage is historical after this executable correction."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T14:01:58.044Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh revised-source receipts: test-local-mur113a4-l5wbvk (this owner, 232/232 focused cases), test-local-mur125gz-ktaxrb (this owner, docstring/link and edited transport/fs/SDK lint gates), and test-local-mur11vg3-grwuow (canonical pm-gh1364, all four configured TypeScript projects, relevant ESLint and unchanged SDK import boundary) pass. The extra isolated standalone unit-file type probe is outside those configured gates: both unchanged HEAD and revised fixtures emit the same 15 pre-existing legacy diagnostics, with no new diagnostics after line-coordinate normalization; retain that limitation rather than labeling the extra probe a pass. Exact edited settings source/test ESLint and strict source-project TSC pass in the isolated copy. Current artifacts remain below the unchanged 20,000,000-byte ceiling (19,982,851 bytes, 1,745 files, no maps), tracked-file secrets scan and whitespace checks pass. Fresh whole-source coverage is pending its single producing command."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T14:06:51.287Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh current-built CLI manual acceptance passed in an owned temporary cwd with both tracker roots isolated: eight contained/external schema mutate/complete cases across extensions enabled/disabled, requested unprefixed target diagnostics, ordered update/comment/strict closure, actual apply, and committed replay. Eleven zero-exclusion full file/directory/mode/byte inventories remain unchanged for previews, including real project/global focus, claim/history, context usage, telemetry events/state and caches; missing item_format remains absent in both settings and schemas remain absent. Preview requested id manual-target is decorated as index0/opupdate/idmanual-target; normal apply retains invalid_argument_value/usage2 without promising preview decoration. The earlier overstrict apply-decoration oracle is preserved as a failed harness assertion, followed by corrected acceptance against the documented staged-only contract. Ordered apply reaches committed/closed; replay reports validated=false/replayed_committed_plan and preserves all bytes. Temporary directory removed; all frozen source hashes match. Linux Node26.9 real built CLI proof, previews opted out of delivery; this establishes neither fresh package reinstall nor remote telemetry correlation. Canonical source hashes: settings7e8eecd185e155e3ab2e823bffc53c2c0dcf241388ca7c972367546303201e5f, CLI main6579be7c20c5f6613d53abec1b06ea9cfdee60d3ec920a1249e497c5015ae4f6; private evidence receiptSHA2568b422a5a8529a5400c331ab66ddaae050bec7ddef4c9e475cfb06b142d5d4fb9."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T14:14:26.081Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Current-source whole-coverage attempt test-local-mur1l8gp-l1icak (canonical producing owner pm-gh1364) failed: 9594 cases passed, one existing release-readiness-runtime read-only transport parity case timed out at the unchanged 30000ms ceiling, two Windows-only cases skipped. No valid coverage summary exists and no coverage measurements will be attached. The failing owner and source connection require focused investigation; overlapping artifact/manual work is a possible resource factor, not an established cause. A fresh complete command, if justified by focused evidence, must retain the same four workers, zero test retries and unchanged timeout/coverage gates. Preserve this failed producing row and its actual stderr."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T14:19:31.023Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Read-only timeout investigation found no validated production defect: release-readiness-runtime.spec.ts, complete runner/temporary workspace/worker helpers, src/cli/main.ts, runtime selection, Vitest config and sandbox runner are SHA-identical to successful fb7 receipts. The failed parity case exercises ordinary reads and never selects the new structured-preview configuration-only branch. Distinct worker/source transport assertions remain valuable; no test deletion, helper rewrite or policy weakening is justified. Its fresh instrumented single-case pass is 5701ms under the unchanged30000ms limit; cold import/resource variation remains unproven, and overlapping work lacks per-case timing attribution. The original failed whole row retains its actual outcome and no coverage measurements."
  - created_at: "2026-10-02T14:19:32.211Z"
    author: "harness:codex"
    text: "Fresh source-boundary reliability observation at2026-10-02T14:12:39Z: required Sentry/telemetry gate passes for unbrained/pm-cli with live access, 14-day zero critical/high/blocking issues, seven-day finish error rate1.28% and zero missing error-code rows. Current telemetry is enabled without test/environment suppression; flush progressed3→2 queued entries with a fresh successful flush timestamp14:12:38.984Z and no failure. This is partial queue progress, not an empty/drained queue. Fresh24h unresolved Sentry issues and1h trace queries both return no rows. Aggregate reliability and local flush observations do not prove per-command collector correlation or OTel/all-action delivery, which remain unverified and distinct from source/coverage proof."
learnings[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-02T06:22:17.080Z","harness:codex","Snapshot ownership follows semantic inputs, not directory names: preserve custom registered item folders, captured schemas, context-intent declarations, and the canonical focused-parent session even under transient namespaces. Pure configuration discovery prevents source scaffolding, captured-byte checks catch discovery races, and committed journal replay must disclose that no fresh step validation occurred. CLI/MCP add transport proof while real SDK persistence owns lifecycle semantics."
  "2026-10-02T07:24:44.212Z","harness:codex","A non-writing SDK preview does not guarantee a non-writing CLI dry-run: command registration, extension discovery, author lookup and post-action preparation can call the normal settings hydrator before or after staging. A real CLI boundary must prove that missing configured source/external schemas are neither created nor followed; preinitializing those fixtures hides the defect. Keep startup reads scoped to the selected source root while allowing normal staged hydration and later apply behavior."
  "2026-10-02T09:59:05.127Z","harness:codex","A non-writing preview must cover CLI startup and error cleanup, not only the staged SDK transaction. Protect conservative literal candidates while discovering configuration, then settle only the invocation-owned policy from the actual parser command and effective inherited options before host preparation. Required extension values, namespace flags and parser failures make cloned grammars unsafe. Keep caller scopes composable and prove ordinary apply still performs hydration, identity and migration work. Use published flag contracts rather than widening private-import allowlists; negative controls must isolate the exact arity or consent regression."
  "2026-10-02T13:11:51.358Z","harness:codex",Retained-state oracles must distinguish canonical session and telemetry state from allowed queue/cache writes. Seed actual focus and prove the oracle rejects genuine unexpected persisted writes. Descriptor entry checks and portable fingerprints do not provide kernel path pinning; document trusted-stable workspace assumptions and platform-specific flags without disabling supported Windows behavior.
  "2026-10-02T14:01:19.892Z","harness:codex","When an absence-aware caller validates an entry before opening it, disappearance can still occur at open: catch only native ENOENT/ENOTDIR at that caller. Preserve permission, symlink/special-file and malformed-input failures. Real filesystem controls at the validated-entry boundary prove both fallback and security behavior without manufacturing error outputs. Keep an actual spawned shipped-launcher path in the existing CLI matrix alongside source instrumentation."
